WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.032
Line 3 stands in hall B, but too many jobs are still cancelled.

2
00:00:05.808 --> 00:00:08.211
The plant manager asks you for advice.

3
00:00:09.243 --> 00:00:10.903
He pays for your advice.

4
00:00:11.714 --> 00:00:15.000
That makes your role different from that of a project manager.

5
00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:18.635
We follow the assignment from start to farewell,

6
00:00:18.774 --> 00:00:20.620
through the four topics of the module.

7
00:00:21.927 --> 00:00:24.319
The first topic is proposal and price.

8
00:00:25.045 --> 00:00:27.506
A proposal wins on its first page.

9
00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:32.398
That page holds his problem, in his own words and numbers.

10
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.639
Your method comes later.

11
00:00:35.764 --> 00:00:39.699
Then come the outcome, the price and what he has to deliver himself.

12
00:00:40.689 --> 00:00:42.825
You put two or three options to him.

13
00:00:43.615 --> 00:00:46.414
Then he chooses how to buy it, and not whether.

14
00:00:47.452 --> 00:00:51.005
For the proposal we use a diagnostic phase and a baseline.

15
00:00:52.306 --> 00:00:55.789
The second topic is the relationship as a trusted advisor.

16
00:00:56.525 --> 00:00:59.114
He has to dare to tell you what really worries him.

17
00:01:00.112 --> 00:01:01.865
He cannot judge your method yet.

18
00:01:02.612 --> 00:01:06.211
He watches small things, such as the minutes on the same day.

19
00:01:07.205 --> 00:01:11.001
Ten small promises kept do more than one brilliant analysis.

20
00:01:12.045 --> 00:01:14.948
Sometimes you advise less work than you could sell.

21
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:17.570
That pays back many times.

22
00:01:18.587 --> 00:01:20.677
For trust we use the trust equation.

23
00:01:22.043 --> 00:01:24.841
The third topic is ethics and independence.

24
00:01:25.548 --> 00:01:27.870
Only the client pays for your advice.

25
00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:32.150
A supplier offers you money for each client you send him.

26
00:01:32.871 --> 00:01:36.551
Then the client can no longer tell whether it bent your advice.

27
00:01:37.637 --> 00:01:40.748
Sometimes you must tell him what he does not want to hear.

28
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.187
First the facts, then your conclusion, then your advice.

29
00:01:46.302 --> 00:01:49.959
You also see his figures and the stop times per employee.

30
00:01:50.638 --> 00:01:52.925
What you learn at his plant stays there.

31
00:01:53.949 --> 00:01:57.595
For that data we use data minimisation and pseudonymising.

32
00:01:58.903 --> 00:02:01.910
The fourth topic is growing the client and the practice.

33
00:02:02.609 --> 00:02:05.477
You hand over the results and name what else you saw.

34
00:02:06.497 --> 00:02:10.677
Do the work so well and so visibly that the next problem comes to you.

35
00:02:11.636 --> 00:02:14.272
A new client can take months of meetings.

36
00:02:15.004 --> 00:02:17.257
Established advisors therefore get most of

37
00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.672
their work from people who already know them.

38
00:02:20.655 --> 00:02:24.695
A result that people can repeat in one sentence brings referrals.

39
00:02:25.693 --> 00:02:29.362
For your own practice we use positioning and billable days.

40
00:02:30.659 --> 00:02:31.507
It connects.

41
00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:35.007
A proposal about his problem, trust you earn,

42
00:02:35.216 --> 00:02:38.014
independent advice and a client who comes back.

43
00:02:39.028 --> 00:02:42.650
After the diagnostic phase he decides whether it goes on.

44
00:02:43.975 --> 00:02:45.693
This is the map of Projects.

45
00:02:46.404 --> 00:02:51.036
The consulting craft is the second station of Portfolio and consulting.

46
00:02:52.086 --> 00:02:55.233
This module has four topics, each with four levels.

47
00:02:56.238 --> 00:02:59.257
Start with proposal and price, at Basics level.

48
00:03:00.284 --> 00:03:02.304
At Working knowledge you add day rate,

49
00:03:02.478 --> 00:03:05.891
collaborative role, processor agreement and utilisation.

50
00:03:06.912 --> 00:03:12.183
At Advanced you add success fee, resistance, the newspaper test and a point of view.

51
00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.323
At Expert you add risk allowance,

52
00:03:15.509 --> 00:03:19.108
humble inquiry, the termination clause and leverage.

53
00:03:20.134 --> 00:03:24.198
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
